================================================================================
Maven pre-check - verbatim evidence
harness/artifacts/logs/maven-preflight.log
================================================================================

WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES

  That the Maven the mandated build wrapper would use was ALREADY the version the
  pinned pom requires, so ./build/mvn triggered no download and this run installed
  nothing (AAP 0.4.3, 0.8.1). The check is a PRE-check by design: the wrapper reads
  <maven.version> from the root pom and downloads an apache-maven distribution into
  build/ whenever the Maven it detects differs, and that download would be an
  installation this run is forbidden to perform. Discovering it afterwards would be
  too late, and .gitignore:39 already ignores build/apache-maven*, so it would also
  be invisible to git.

  RESULT: PASS. The resolvable Maven is 3.9.11, the pom requires 3.9.11, the two
  are equal, the wrapper's download branch was therefore unreachable, and no
  apache-maven distribution exists under the build tree's build/ directory.

  WHY THIS FILE WAS WRITTEN A SECOND TIME WITHIN THE RUN

  The pre-check is a property of the tree about to be built, and this run built the
  full reactor a second time: the tree the earlier build produced was deleted with
  the scratch directory of the clone that ran it, so the artifacts the graph must be
  built over no longer existed. The graph the AAP requires this run to create can
  only be created over artifacts that exist, so the build was re-run into a private
  clone of the same pin and this file records THAT build's pre-check. Every figure
  here was measured against the tree named in STEP 1.
